## Context

Audit finding F5 (`verification/SITTER-LIFECYCLE-AUDIT-2026-09-12.md`).

The on-disk cache is keyed on the host's processor stamps
(`resource://zotero/document-worker/metadata.json`), and every row whose
`versions` differ is dropped on load. Those stamps move on point releases: this
repository's own reading is `SDT_SCHEMA_VERSION` 1.1.0 -> 1.2.0 and the PDF
processor stamp 3 -> 14 between the 10.0 build and 10.0.2 — eleven stamps across
three point releases (`plugins/sdt-sitter/RELEASE-NOTES.md`).

So the ordinary consequence of a Zotero update is a total cache invalidation and
a full re-census. The plugin survives that correctly. What it does not do is
explain it: `emit('cache-load', …)` reports the rows *kept* and never the rows
dropped, so a post-upgrade session is indistinguishable from a broken one from
the user's side — everything done again, no reason given. 0771 adds a second
occasion for the same silence: a cache written before its row stamp existed is
dropped once, wholesale.

## Relevant files

- `plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js` — the cache read loop and `cache-load`
- `tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs` — the existing cache-load scenarios
- `SPEC.md` §5.2.7 — the sitter's surfaces; check whether a new line needs
  declaring there, as the census classes already are

## Actions

1. Count the rows skipped, by reason (foreign pack versions, foreign row
   format, malformed), and carry the counts in the `cache-load` record beside
   the rows kept.
2. When rows were dropped for a version or format mismatch, say so once in the
   window: the host's text processors changed, so earlier observations no longer
   apply and the pass is being re-measured. One sentence, composed once, in the
   voice the panel already uses.
3. Respect the string rules: `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py` bans "document", "pack"
   and the rest from user-facing text and requires each UI site to read from one
   composer. Read those tests before writing the sentence.

## Test

- Red first: a cache whose every row carries foreign versions loads zero rows
  and the window says nothing about why.
- The counts reach the `cache-load` record, by reason.
- The sentence appears after a version-mismatch drop and NOT after an ordinary
  empty-cache first run — a first install has nothing to explain.
- The sentence is gone on the next activation, which has a current cache.

## Verification

- [ ] `node tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs`
- [ ] `python3 -m pytest tests/test_sdt_sitter.py -q` — the string guards
- [ ] `python3 verification/probes/sdt_sitter_bootstrap_mutants.py`
- [ ] `make check`

## Invariants

- No new durable state, no new pref.
- The census verdicts do not move: this is a reading about the cache, not about
  the library.

## Exit criteria

- A session that dropped its cache says why, once, in words a reader can read.
